# From "Color Breathing" (Wave II - Threshold, CD2-4) -- filed at F10, where
# the tape itself sits, despite the wave. Three separate one-breath tools,
# same structure each time: inhale, hold with the color and intent in mind,
# exhale to release it.
#
# **These are taught here and used later.** The tape is explicit about it --
# "From this moment on, whenever you desire to perform a physical act... all
# you need do is" -- and every consequence is future indicative: "when you
# exhale the breath from your lungs and open your eyes, you will be able to
# immediately perform the physical act you have pictured".
#
# An earlier draft flattened that into the present imperative: "Exhale, open
# your eyes, and perform it." Read aloud to someone lying down at Focus 10
# with the bed running, that is an instruction to open their eyes and get up,
# ninety seconds after being told to relax. The opening line said "whenever
# you need them", but a frame three recipes back does not survive a direct
# command. The grammar is the safety here, so it follows the tape's.

@segment  color-breathing
@title    Color Breathing
@levels   F10
@duration ~2m

say Three ways to use color, on a single breath. Learn them here; they are for later, in ordinary waking life, whenever you need them.
pause 5
say The first reduces an emotional charge, down to where it is no longer harmful. You close your eyes, inhale deeply, and hold the breath, thinking of calming, cleansing green.
pause 6
say As you exhale slowly, the green pushes the excess charge down through your body and out through the soles of your feet, leaving you calm, confident, and serene.
pause 8
say The second charges your body for strength, speed and coordination before a physical act. You inhale, hold the breath, think of the act, then the strong energy of red.
pause 6
say When you exhale and open your eyes, you will perform it stronger, faster, and more coordinated than before.
pause 8
say The third helps any part of your body toward balance. You inhale, hold the breath, and think of cool, healing purple. With your eyes closed you look at the part that needs it, and send the purple there, saying in your mind: heal, balance.
pause 8
say When you exhale and open your eyes, that part begins restoring itself immediately, more completely than before.
pause 8
say The more you use any of these, the easier and more effective they become.
pause 6
